1
00:00:00,079 --> 00:00:02,980
Open Mapping and choose Map Icon Legend.

2
00:00:03,529 --> 00:00:06,329
A call's marker follows its type and priority.

3
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:10,029
A unit's marker follows its type and current status.

4
00:00:10,479 --> 00:00:13,829
A person's marker follows an applicable role and status.

5
00:00:14,270 --> 00:00:16,530
Staffing levels do not change the icon.

6
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:20,000
Our fictional examples are the Warehouse alarm,

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Reserve Engine 51 and

8
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,709
Matthew Casey. Keep their names visible while comparing symbols.

9
00:00:26,190 --> 00:00:29,659
The colors and artwork identify different things, so match a

10
00:00:29,659 --> 00:00:33,680
marker to its named entity before drawing an operational conclusion.

11
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:36,609
From Department Types, edit Structure Fire.

12
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:41,340
The Map Icon selector supplies a built-in choice; Custom icon

13
00:00:41,340 --> 00:00:43,180
supplies the uploaded alternative.

14
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,390
Choose File and select the training fire image.

15
00:00:46,819 --> 00:00:51,409
Read the Icon guidelines: supported formats are PNG, JPEG,

16
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:54,169
GIF and WebP, up to one megabyte.

17
00:00:54,590 --> 00:00:56,399
SVG is not supported.

18
00:00:56,860 --> 00:01:00,659
Compare Preview on Light map, Dark map and In a list.

19
00:01:01,049 --> 00:01:04,159
A bold transparent square stays readable when small.

20
00:01:04,590 --> 00:01:06,740
Choose Update, then reopen the form.

21
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:10,490
Showing the current custom icon confirms the stored result,

22
00:01:10,619 --> 00:01:12,340
rather than just a selected file.

23
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:14,470
Choose Priority map icons.

24
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:16,170
Find the Urgent row.

25
00:01:16,550 --> 00:01:21,459
Priority and Map color describe the actual setting; Default shows its fallback.

26
00:01:21,759 --> 00:01:26,099
The file selected here happens to be named call-emergency, but

27
00:01:26,129 --> 00:01:27,959
it is being uploaded for Urgent.

28
00:01:28,309 --> 00:01:30,959
A filename does not change the call's priority.

29
00:01:31,389 --> 00:01:33,070
Use that row's Upload button.

30
00:01:33,469 --> 00:01:37,010
Icon saved and the image under Uploaded icon show the stored

31
00:01:37,010 --> 00:01:39,549
replacement; Remove is now available.

32
00:01:39,879 --> 00:01:43,139
The named Warehouse alarm now shows that replacement on Mapping.

33
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:47,590
In the legend, Routine and Emergency still use the type's base image

34
00:01:47,590 --> 00:01:48,970
with their priority badges.

35
00:01:49,159 --> 00:01:51,969
Open Units and check Reserve Engine 51.

36
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:56,319
Its Type is Engine and its starting Status is Out of Service.

37
00:01:56,750 --> 00:02:00,699
Engine 51 is a different unit and remains Released in this recording.

38
00:02:01,199 --> 00:02:02,710
Edit the Engine unit type.

39
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:06,900
Review Actions, which is set to Standard Actions, then choose the

40
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:08,990
training image under Custom icon.

41
00:02:09,449 --> 00:02:13,429
Compare the light, dark and list previews before choosing Update.

42
00:02:13,929 --> 00:02:17,220
Reopen the definition to confirm the current saved icon.

43
00:02:17,679 --> 00:02:21,140
The reserve unit's map initially shows that blue base image

44
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:22,570
with an unavailable badge.

45
00:02:22,950 --> 00:02:26,509
Changing an icon definition does not change the unit's status.

46
00:02:26,669 --> 00:02:28,949
Open Status map icons for Engine.

47
00:02:29,449 --> 00:02:32,920
Choose the Available row and select the green training image.

48
00:02:33,339 --> 00:02:37,249
Notice that Map color follows the operational meaning, while the status

49
00:02:37,249 --> 00:02:39,009
label has its own display color.

50
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:42,160
Choose Upload and confirm Icon saved.

51
00:02:42,570 --> 00:02:45,670
This replacement applies to Engine units while Available.

52
00:02:46,109 --> 00:02:50,000
For the disposable reserve example, open Set Status,

53
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,060
choose Available,

54
00:02:51,459 --> 00:02:56,160
keep Destination at None, add a clear training Note and choose Save.

55
00:02:56,570 --> 00:02:58,629
The Units grid confirms Available.

56
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:01,209
The map then shows the green replacement.

57
00:03:01,599 --> 00:03:05,849
Its station point was supplied separately as declared simulated fixture setup.

58
00:03:06,209 --> 00:03:11,610
This dialog did not collect GPS or inherit station coordinates; an entity without

59
00:03:11,610 --> 00:03:14,059
a permitted location may have no marker.

60
00:03:14,299 --> 00:03:16,740
Open Personnel Roles and view Officer.

61
00:03:17,299 --> 00:03:20,890
Matthew Casey, Stella Kidd and Christopher Herrmann are already

62
00:03:20,890 --> 00:03:22,550
members in this fictional department.

63
00:03:23,050 --> 00:03:26,490
Edit the role, choose the training image under Custom icon,

64
00:03:26,870 --> 00:03:29,109
inspect Preview and choose Save.

65
00:03:29,529 --> 00:03:32,580
Reopen it to confirm Showing the current custom icon.

66
00:03:33,090 --> 00:03:35,789
Back on Personnel Roles, read Role order.

67
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:40,350
A person uses the first role they hold, in this order, that has an icon.

68
00:03:40,780 --> 00:03:42,129
Officer is fourth here.

69
00:03:42,539 --> 00:03:45,819
If you deliberately change the order, use Save order.

70
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:49,409
No role order or membership is changed in this example.

71
00:03:49,670 --> 00:03:52,530
From Officer, choose Status map icons.

72
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:56,100
Find Standing By and select its training replacement.

73
00:03:56,469 --> 00:04:01,030
This combination belongs to that role and that personnel status; it does not

74
00:04:01,030 --> 00:04:03,389
apply to every member regardless of role.

75
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:09,499
Choose Upload and check Icon saved, Uploaded icon and Remove on the same row.

76
00:04:10,009 --> 00:04:12,659
Return to the map and filter to Matthew Casey.

77
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:16,489
The named marker shows the gray replacement from the Standing By row.

78
00:04:16,870 --> 00:04:20,130
Keep the visible name with the symbol so a nearby person's marker

79
00:04:20,130 --> 00:04:22,050
cannot be mistaken for Casey's.

80
00:04:22,189 --> 00:04:25,749
Use Map Icon Legend to explain how a symbol is chosen.

81
00:04:26,150 --> 00:04:29,270
An upload for the exact priority or status wins.

82
00:04:29,690 --> 00:04:34,229
Otherwise the type's or role's own upload can carry a meaning-colored badge.

83
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:37,189
Otherwise a built-in pin uses that style.

84
00:04:37,660 --> 00:04:40,469
Compare the Structure Fire row across priorities.

85
00:04:40,860 --> 00:04:44,750
Then compare Engine across statuses: Available has its

86
00:04:44,750 --> 00:04:48,510
specific replacement while the other states use the base and badge.

87
00:04:48,879 --> 00:04:52,110
Finally compare Officer across personnel statuses.

88
00:04:52,459 --> 00:04:55,770
The legend also explains that a member On Unit can take the

89
00:04:55,770 --> 00:04:57,419
color of their unit's status.

90
00:04:57,759 --> 00:05:01,610
That is a reference example here, not a newly performed crew assignment.

91
00:05:01,810 --> 00:05:05,119
Restore the disposable reserve unit through Set Status.

92
00:05:05,519 --> 00:05:10,039
Choose Out of Service, wait for Destination to settle at None, add the

93
00:05:10,039 --> 00:05:12,440
training restoration Note and choose Save.

94
00:05:12,919 --> 00:05:17,520
The Units grid confirms Out of Service, while Engine 51 remains Released.

95
00:05:17,899 --> 00:05:21,419
For this recording, the original fictional station point is restored

96
00:05:21,419 --> 00:05:23,770
again as separate simulated setup data.

97
00:05:24,159 --> 00:05:29,000
The actual map now shows the blue Engine base with its black unavailable badge,

98
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:33,879
matching the legend. The status changes used the normal application controls; neither

99
00:05:33,879 --> 00:05:38,100
setup step demonstrates device GPS or an operational response.

100
00:05:38,290 --> 00:05:43,140
Test a reversible fallback by returning to Structure Fire's Urgent row and choosing

101
00:05:43,189 --> 00:05:45,500
Remove for this disposable override.

102
00:05:45,950 --> 00:05:49,870
Icon removed appears, and Uploaded icon returns to None.

103
00:05:50,250 --> 00:05:52,359
The call's priority has not changed.

104
00:05:52,779 --> 00:05:54,000
Revisit the legend and

105
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,250
the named Warehouse alarm.

106
00:05:55,670 --> 00:05:59,090
Both now show the base fire image with the high-priority badge.

107
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:02,490
The original training calls remain open and unchanged.

108
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:07,389
Finish by recording a small, consistent set of symbols and meanings, and retain

109
00:06:07,389 --> 00:06:09,610
labels where an icon could be ambiguous.

110
00:06:09,969 --> 00:06:13,530
These are actual Core browser views; native-device appearance

111
00:06:13,559 --> 00:06:14,990
is not demonstrated here.

